# type(scope): subject
#
# One commit, one concern - application code (classroom_project/), docs
# (docs/, README.md), or chore/tooling, never mixed in the same commit.
# GitHub's per-path file listing shows whichever commit last touched
# that path, so a mixed commit mislabels a directory with an unrelated
# message.
#
# Types: feat fix docs chore refactor test perf build ci
# Subject: imperative mood, lower case after the colon, no trailing
# period, under 72 characters.
#
# Body (optional, blank line above it): the why, not the what.
